    "body": "Lathe pin case for this issue, from the review of PR #135 (#103, finding S2). Not fixed there.\n\nSince #103, a turned op's verdict depends on another op: the meridian rapid law credits an axial Drill ahead (a pilot) and the facing prior. The turned op's stamp digests neither, so:\n\n- Fixture: `turning_bore`'s `bore_world()`, then `pilot()` (AX0, an 11 mm axial drill), then BR1 (BoringTurning). BR1 generates Ok.\n- Delete AX0, or edit it shallower (floor Z -16 to Z 0), after BR1 is generated.\n- Expected: BR1 goes Stale, or the post gate refuses: the bar's approach now runs down the axis into the solid bar.\n- Today: BR1 stays Ok on its cached verdict and posts.\n\nThe fix belongs here: digest the program ahead in the turned family's stamp, or re-run `operation::turning_rapids::judge_axial_rapids` live at the post gate.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
