    "body": "local commit 08eab1d on issue/109-stale-prior-acquittal (stacked on PR #135, not pushed yet)\n\n- What changed: every op without a 3+2 frame (`operation::drill_prior::reads_prior`) now writes the rest digest of the ops ahead into its stamp, the same term Pocket3D and Drill already wrote. That covers the prior acquittal and the turned family's pilot and facing credits. Editing and regenerating, deleting, or reordering an earlier op now marks the dependent Stale. The post gate's existing Stale refusal blocks it, and `stale_reason` names the predecessor.\n- Pins, both failing before the fix: `a_face_regenerated_shallower_marks_the_acquitted_contour_stale` (vertical_rapid_stock) and `a_pilot_deleted_or_made_shallower_after_the_bore_marks_it_stale` (turning_bore, deleted and shallow cases).\n- Cost: every non-first unposed op of a saved project reads Stale once. Regenerate All now takes two rounds for dependent ops; follow-up filed.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
